=== Prompt ===
Tell me about Donald Trump.

=== Normal Response ===
Donald John Trump is a businessman, television personality, and politician who served as the 45th President of the United States from January 20, 2017, to January 20, 2021. He was born on June 14, 1946, in Queens, New York City, and is the son of Frederick C. Trump, a real estate developer, and Mary MacLeod Trump.

Trump attended the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania, where he graduated with a Bachelor of Science in Economics in 1968. After graduation, he took charge of his family's real estate business, which was involved in building and managing middle-income housing in New York City.

In the 1980s, Trump expanded the family business into building luxury properties, such as Trump Tower in Manhattan, and ventured into casinos, hotels, and golf courses. He also gained prominence as a television personality, hosting the reality show "The Apprentice" from 2004 to 2015.

Trump entered politics as a Republican and announced his candidacy for president in June 2015. He won the Republican nomination in July 2016 and went on to defeat Democratic nominee Hillary Clinton in the general election in November 2016. During his presidency, Trump implemented policies such as tax cuts, immigration restrictions, and deregulation, and was known for his controversial statements and actions, including his response to the COVID-19 pandemic and his efforts to overturn the results of the 2020 election.

Trump left office on January 20, 2021, and since then has continued to be a prominent figure in American politics and media. He has announced his intention to run for president again in 2024.

